    description: 'Late-1990s and early-2000s American teen-targeted pop subgenre developed through the post-Mickey-Mouse-Club Britney Spears, Christina Aguilera, *NSYNC, Backstreet Boys cycle. Characterized by sophisticated R&B-and-dance-influenced commercial-radio production, choreographed-music-video presentation aesthetic, and explicit teen-audience demographic targeting. The Cheiron Studios (Stockholm, Max Martin) production-team inaugurated the canonical Swedish-pop-production aesthetic that defined much of late-1990s teen pop.',
