    description: 'The Roma-Balkan svatba wedding-music tradition continuous from 19th-20th century Roma musical-professionalization across Bulgaria, Macedonia, Serbia, Romania, Turkey, and broader Balkan zones; defined by Balkan-aksak odd-meter rhythmic vocabulary (7/8, 9/8, 11/8 wedding-dance meters including ručenica and lesno), Eastern-modal vocabulary with maqam-style microtonal inflection, virtuosic accordion-and-clarinet-and-fiddle ensemble foreground with brass-band (trumpet-and-saxophone-led) festive arrangement, characteristic Roma cocek dance-form, ululation-and-shouted-vocal celebratory practice, dense ensemble-texture with sustained-energy dance-foreground spanning multiple-hour wedding-feast performance. The Goran Bregović 1989-onward film-and-soundtrack work canonized the form for international audiences; the Slavic Soul Party and Boban Marković Orkestar are the modern-codified-Balkan-brass-wedding reference.',
