    description: 'The Romanian harvest-carol (colinde de seceriş, "harvest-colinde" — though the broader colinde-tradition is canonically associated with Christmas-and-New-Year, the harvest-context colinde-rep is documented as a distinct seasonal sub-tradition) tradition continuous from premodern Romanian-agricultural village-labor practice through 19th-century Romanian-folklorist documentation (Vasile Alecsandri Poezii populare ale românilor 1852-1853 and Constantin Brăiloiu mid-20th-century ethnomusicological-documentation) through 20th-century Béla Bartók-and-Constantin-Brăiloiu canonical-ethnomusicology (Bartók\'s 1909-1917 Romanian-folk-collection documented the Romanian harvest-and-ritual-song corpus extensively) into modern Romanian-folk-revival continuous practice. Defined by unaccompanied group-vocal arrangement, Romanian-language text register, characteristic Romanian-folk modal vocabulary, characteristic women\'s-group seasonal-labor performance-context.',
    exemplars: ['Vasile Alecsandri — Poezii populare ale românilor 1852-1853 (canonical foundational)', 'Constantin Brăiloiu — Romanian Folklore Institute mid-20th-century canonical', 'Béla Bartók — 1909-1917 Romanian-folk-collection canonical', 'Maria Tănase — canonical 20th-century Romanian-folk-vocal', 'Modern Romanian-village colinde-and-harvest-carol continuous-living tradition'],
