    description: 'The Bengali bhatiali (boatmen\'s song) tradition continuous from premodern Bengali-riverine-and-Sundarbans-delta boatmen labor practice (the Padma-Ganges-Brahmaputra-Meghna river-delta of Bengal supported extensive boat-trade and fisher-population) through 19th-20th century Tagore-era literary-elevation (Tagore composed extensively in the bhatiali idiom under his Rabindra-Sangeet broader-song project) into modern Bengali-and-Bangladeshi continuous practice. The bhatiali is the canonical Bengali downstream-rowing-song integrating long-held-vocal phrases matched to slow downstream-rowing strokes (distinct from the uptempo upstream-rowing-song traditions). Defined by dotara-and-ektara-and-voice arrangement, Bengali-language text register, Hindustani-folk modal vocabulary, characteristic long-melismatic-phrase boat-context.',
    exemplars: ['Rabindra-Sangeet bhatiali-style canonical (Rabindranath Tagore)', 'Abbasuddin Ahmed — canonical 20th-century Bengali bhatiali vocalist', 'Abdul Alim — canonical Bangladeshi bhatiali', '"Allah meghde paani de" canonical Bengali bhatiali', 'Bengali Padma-river boatmen continuous-living tradition'],
    crossRefs: ['fieldWork.eastAsian', 'seaShanty.atlantic', 'lullaby.southAsian'],
