    description: 'The San (Khoisan) hunting-and-trance song tradition continuous from premodern Kalahari-Desert hunter-gatherer practice through 20th-21st century continuous performance (where it survives — the San cultural-practice is increasingly endangered with documented language-and-cultural-erosion) into modern San practice across Botswana, Namibia, and South Africa; the San hunting-song tradition integrates trance-dance with hunting-magic and game-divination ritual (the canonical San trance-dance documented by Lorna Marshall and Megan Biesele). Defined by unaccompanied women\'s-group-vocal clapping-percussion arrangement with men entering the trance-dance circle, characteristic Khoisan-click-language text register with extensive click-consonants and ideophones, characteristic narrow-range polyphonic vocal arrangement.',
    exemplars: ['Lorna Marshall — The !Kung of Nyae Nyae 1976 canonical', 'Megan Biesele — Women Like Meat 1993 canonical-ethnography', 'San trance-dance traditional continuous-living tradition', 'Eland Bull Song canonical San hunting-magic', 'Kxao Tami!Ai — San bushman canonical-tradition-bearer'],
    crossRefs: ['huntingSong.arctic', 'ritualDevotional.indigenous', 'huntingSong.centralAsian'],
    status: 'documented',
