    description: 'The Sami vuolle (Lule-Sami "yoik" variant) and broader Sami domestic-labor song tradition continuous from premodern Sami reindeer-herding-and-domestic-textile practice across the Sápmi-region through colonial-era continuous performance into modern Sami-cultural-revival; the vuolle is the Lule-Sami yoik-variant distinct from the Northern-Sami juoiggus, with the broader Sami domestic-song repertoire covering child-rearing, sewing, and domestic-textile-labor coordination. Defined by unaccompanied solo-vocal narrative-and-recitative arrangement, Lule-Sami-language text register, narrow-range pentatonic-leaning melodic vocabulary.',
