    description: 'The Korean baennoraega (뱃노래, "boatmen\'s song") and broader Korean women\'s-domestic-labor song tradition continuous from premodern Korean-rural domestic-labor practice through Joseon-dynasty continuous performance into modern Korean-folk-revival; the baennoraega coordinates fishing-boat-rowing while parallel women\'s-domestic-labor songs accompanied weaving, grain-grinding, and household-textile labor. The canonical Korean min\'yo (folk-song) tradition integrates both maritime and domestic-textile sub-genres with characteristic Korean-minsogak-mode melodic vocabulary. Defined by unaccompanied women\'s-or-men\'s solo-or-small-group vocal arrangement, Korean-Hangul text register, characteristic Korean-folk modal vocabulary (yukjabaegi-tori, gyeongtori, mereumdori), characteristic regional-Korean dialect variation.',
    exemplars: ['"Arirang" canonical Korean min\'yo broader tradition', '"Baennoraega" canonical Korean rowing-song traditional', 'Kim So-hee — canonical 20th-century Korean min\'yo vocalist', 'Modern Korean min\'yo-revival continuous-tradition', 'Korean-rural women\'s domestic-labor song continuous-living tradition'],
