  "british_math_rock": {"parent":"distortedRock.experimental","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":1,"meter":-1,"density":0,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":0,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":-1},"description":"This is a song-facing math-rock model, not an automatically instrumental national style. The arrangement lets intricate tapped guitar and bass-baritone lines remain distinct beneath a sung melody. Uneven groupings and changes of accent provide motion without requiring one fixed unusual time signature. It differs from the selected British post-rock model by favoring compact, articulated counterpoint over sustained guitar/synth washes.","exemplars":["TTNG — Disappointment Island","TTNG — 13.0.0.0.0","Delta Sleep","Orchards"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
