  "canadian_shoegaze": {"parent":"distortedRock.alternative","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":2,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":2,"intensity":0,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"The selected production model places magnetically sustained guitar notes through unstable tape-style echo around a sung band arrangement, with an electronic autoharp color retained as its own instrument. Parts are assembled and refined in the studio rather than assumed to be one uninterrupted live take. Omnichord appears on a specific album track, not every song. The default is a representative combination of documented album-era practices; other Canadian shoegaze branches need not share its guest instrument or falsetto lead.","exemplars":["The Besnard Lakes — The Besnard Lakes Are the Roaring Night","The Besnard Lakes — The Lonely Moan","The Besnard Lakes — And This Is What We Call Progress"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
