  "canadian_rockabilly": {"parent":"distortedRock.regional","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"The default highlights the percussive double-bass attack alongside semi-hollow guitar resonance and an organ layer. Its selected2010s branch draws on country, punk and rock-and-roll practice, not a claim that Canadian rockabilly is uniformly horror-themed or reproduces1950s instrumentation. Band singing and organ remain audible roles; church ritual is not inferred from the player’s stage name or the word gospel in a timbral description.","exemplars":["The Creepshow — Life After Death","The Creepshow — Death at My Door","The Creepshow — Run for Your Life"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "brazilian_post_rock": {"parent":"distortedRock.experimental","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":1,"transmission":0,"improv":1,"soundTech":1,"intensity":0,"voice":-2,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":0},"description":"The arrangement treats rhythm as a property of the whole ensemble, not only the drum kit. Metal-bar mallet attacks contrast with the low reed, brass and amplified strings, with parts developed collectively from small ideas. Players can alternate instruments or layer them in recording; six instrument categories do not assert that every voice sounds continuously in a single live pass. National origin is not used to invent samba percussion or a compulsory regional rhythm.","exemplars":["Hurtmold — Mils Crianças","Hurtmold — Mestro","Hurtmold — Hurtmold","ruído/mm","Labirinto"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "danish_rock": {"parent":"distortedRock.regional","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":0,"improv":1,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":1},"description":"The selected arrangement sets a bright, country-inflected guitar voice against a more driven rhythm-guitar layer, with low-end support from a two-string bass. The unusual bass construction is a documented performer choice, not a requirement for Danish rock. The model draws on the band’s continuing repertoire and first-person guitar accounts rather than reproducing every1989 or later tour setup.","exemplars":["D-A-D — Sleeping My Day Away","D-A-D — No Fuel Left for the Pilgrims","D-A-D — A Prayer for the Loud"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "classical_bass": {"parent":"artMusic.westernCommonPractice","axes":{"harm":2,"pitch":1,"ornament":1,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":2,"improv":-1,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":0,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-2,"cyclicity":-1},"description":"A voice-type discovery entry for classical bass and bass-baritone singers. The authored model selects the intimate art-song side of a documented bass recital: one low singing voice and a concert grand, with natural hall acoustics and restrained processing. The wider scope also includes operatic and oratorio ensembles; it is not a contrabass-instrument category.","exemplars":["Ruggero Raimondi","Ferruccio Furlanetto"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "italian_bass": {"parent":"artMusic.westernCommonPractice","axes":{"harm":2,"pitch":1,"ornament":2,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":2,"improv":-1,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":0,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-2,"cyclicity":-1},"description":"An Italian-origin low classical singer discovery field. This authored recital branch selects bass-voice opera excerpts with piano, sustained projected phrasing and expressive dynamic space. Italian identity does not confine repertoire to Italian-language works, and the category includes bass-baritone practitioners as well as basses.","exemplars":["Ruggero Raimondi","Ferruccio Furlanetto"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "brazilian_thrash_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.thrash","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"A Brazilian geographic thrash-metal field. This authored early-Sepultura branch favors clipped distorted guitar figures, picked bass and driving double-kick kit underneath voice. It retains E-standard guitar tuning from the documented earlier period; later downtuning and percussion experiments remain optional rather than retroactively imposed.","exemplars":["Sepultura"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "brazilian_groove_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"A Brazilian groove-metal discovery field. The authored Chaos AD-informed branch uses whole-step-down guitar, short palm-muted attacks and a weighty kit/bass foundation, leaving more space for rhythmic punctuation than the selected thrash model. The choice does not make all Brazilian metal groove metal or require additional folk percussion in every track.","exemplars":["Sepultura"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "brazilian_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"A national metal discovery scope. This authored modern guitar-band branch combines sustained distorted chords, electric bass, an acoustic kit and voice. It provides a flexible representative ensemble while preserving the wider scene’s thrash, groove, power, progressive and other branches. Extra classical guitar, Hammond and violin in Sepultura’s later arrangements are documented options, not compulsory Brazilian markers.","exemplars":["Sepultura"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "australian_death_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.death","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":2,"meter":2,"density":1,"transmission":0,"improv":1,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":-1},"description":"Australian death-metal discovery scope, with a technical Psycroptic-informed branch. The authored model combines tightly articulated electric guitar, picked bass, rapid acoustic-kit playing and voice. Riff sections develop through guitar/drum interaction, while the recording model allows home overdubs after studio drums. Half-step-down tuning is an authored choice, not attributed to the documented session.","exemplars":["Psycroptic"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
