  "yorkshire_folk": {"parent":"balladPoetry.celticBalladic","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Lead and supporting voices are answered by fiddle and diatonic accordion over plucked double bass. Blooming Heather credits establish these roles; the compact configuration leaves out the record’s electric guitar and orchestral strings, and D/G melodeon rows are an authored choice.","exemplars":["Kate Rusby — Blooming Heather"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "medieval_folk": {"parent":"balladPoetry","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":0,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Layered voices and hurdy-gurdy melody/drone interlock with harp and Irish bouzouki. This selected acoustic branch follows FAUN’s documented quieter concert format and musicians’ actual instruments; it leaves electronic festival production optional rather than pretending it did not exist or making it compulsory.","exemplars":["FAUN — acoustic concert programme"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "italian_folk": {"parent":"balladPoetry","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":1,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Text-led singing and a hand-played jingled frame drum exchange pulse, flourishes and silence. This source-backed Sicilian branch uses the existing frame-drum family with selected regional form/context variants; exact wood, membrane and modern recording setup remain authored choices.","exemplars":["Alfio Antico"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "new_england_americana": {"parent":"functionalSong.country.americana","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Harmony voices, strummed jarana, twin fiddle lines and jawbone percussion form a compact arrangement drawn from the documented Unfruitful session. This authored subset leaves out the record’s additional horsehead fiddle, organs and other colors rather than pretending those instruments were absent.","exemplars":["David Wax Museum — Unfruitful"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "macedonian_folk": {"parent":"improvOnFrame","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":2,"meter":1,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":-2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"An ornamented bagpipe melody sounds over its sustained drone. This solo option follows documented practice; drum accompaniment is possible but not mandatory. Performer-relative tuning avoids imposing an unsupported temperament.","exemplars":["Pece Atanasovski — gajda lineage"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "indie_folk_argentino": {"parent":"balladPoetry.angloSingerSong.indieFolk","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":-1,"intensity":-1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Lead voice, acoustic guitar, Wurlitzer electric piano and cello create a compact chamber-song texture. Si Agua credits establish these roles; using one cello is an authored reduction of a larger string section, with programming and brass left outside this selected configuration.","exemplars":["Mía Maestro — Si Agua"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
