  "minimal_dubstep": {"parent":"bassSystem.ukSoundsystem","axes":{"harm":-1,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":-2,"transmission":1,"improv":0,"soundTech":2,"intensity":0,"voice":-2,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"A sparse sampled-percussion and digital-subtractive-bass setup inspired by early Mala. The producer describes sine-derived bass in Reason, while the contemporary interview documents his sample-based tracks and South London context. The existing Nord-style virtual-analog menu is an authored practical substitute, not a claim about his actual Reason software or a physical analog synthesizer. This instrumental production branch leaves room between events; it does not import the full Cuban live percussion band from his later project or turn every sampled sound into a separate live player.","exemplars":["Mala / Digital Mystikz — early DMZ production practice"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
