  "lapland_hip_hop": {"parent":"mcRhythm.intlHipHop","axes":{"harm":-1,"pitch":-1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":0,"transmission":0,"improv":1,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":2,"timbre":0,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Rhythmic rap sits over a programmed beat and layered virtual-instrument textures. AMOC directly explains that the organic-sounding instruments on Čuđeh were made on a computer. The sampler’s orchestral/virtual-library role is an authored realization of that process, without falsely adding live bowed strings, joik or a ritual drum merely because the artist is Sámi.","exemplars":["AMOC — Čuđeh","Niki Rasmus","Heidi Gauriloff"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "celtic_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.folkMetal","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":2,"meter":0,"density":2,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Celtic metal combines metal-band practice with selected Celtic musical material and instruments rather than one standardized ethnic sound. Cruachan’s Irish branch supplies the model here: electric guitars, bass and drums interact with tin-whistle and fiddle lines, with a harsh vocal layer. Keith Fay describes sustained folk/metal integration, while recording interviews document studio expansion with folk instruments and strings. This authored six-role reduction retains both acoustic melody instruments instead of substituting a generic synthesizer for them.","exemplars":["Cruachan — Irish folk/metal branch around Blood for the Blood God (2014)"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "chinese_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":0,"density":1,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":1,"timbre":1,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Chinese metal includes varied regional and stylistic practices. Tang Dynasty supplies this selected guitar-centered branch: heavy-metal lead/rhythm guitars, bass, drums and melodic singing, informed by Chinese musical and poetic traditions. Co-founder Kaiser Kuo describes the band’s Beijing beginnings and mutual exchange between Chinese music and Western metal. This authored four-role model emphasizes sustained electric lead guitar without assuming that Chinese identity requires traditional acoustic instruments or one universal vocal method.","exemplars":["Tang Dynasty — classic guitar-centered heavy-metal branch"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
