  "chilean_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":-1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Chilean metal is a national scene umbrella, represented by Criminal’s death/thrash and groove-oriented Sacrificio. The label credits vocals/guitars, second guitar, bass and drums and discusses collective rehearsal, rhythmic emphasis and writing/recording in Chile. The authored arrangement gives clipped guitar riffs, bass and live-kit accents a forceful vocal foreground. This is a death/thrash-groove example within Chilean metal; the national category also contains other styles, and differs from the narrower Chilean black-metal allocation. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Criminal — Sacrificio"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
