  "christian_death_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.death","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":-1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":2,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Christian death metal is a faith-and-lyric-defined branch, represented by Mortification’s early death/grind practice. The publisher describes low-tuned, fast and technically forceful music; the documented ensemble centers on guitar, bass/voice and drums. The authored model combines heavy guitar attacks with bass reinforcement, dense drum bursts and harsh lead voice. Christian distinguishes lyrical and community orientation, rather than a different guitar technology or physiological vocal mechanism. This death/grind model is narrower than Christian metal’s broader heavy, power and symphonic branches. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Mortification — Scrolls of the Megilloth"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "christian_doom_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.doom","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":-1,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":0,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Christian doom metal is represented by Doom of Death’s explicitly biblical epic-doom release Valley of Shadows. The band’s own notes describe slow pacing and solemn melody, and credit voice, keyboards, rhythm and lead guitars, bass and drums. The authored realization spaces sustained low guitar chords around a deliberate rhythm section and keyboard support. The Christian boundary is explicitly lyrical; doom here means the slow epic branch, rather than treating every Christian metal ballad as doom. Ceará is the disclosed regional locality, not a claimed exact home city. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Doom of Death — Valley of Shadows"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "christian_power_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.power","axes":{"harm":2,"pitch":1,"ornament":1,"meter":2,"density":2,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Christian power metal is represented by Theocracy’s Athens-based melodic/progressive power-metal practice. The band identifies two guitars, bass, drums and lead/backing vocals, and discusses galloping anthems with explicitly spiritual subject matter. This model uses bright melodic leads above tightly articulated riffs and an energetic rhythm section. Faith-based songwriting defines the Christian qualifier; soaring melody and galloping power-metal arrangement distinguish this chosen branch from Christian death or doom metal. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Theocracy — Mosaic"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "christian_symphonic_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.symphonic","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":1,"density":2,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":2,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Christian symphonic metal is represented here by Renascent’s symphonic extreme-metal branch rather than a universal clean-soprano template. The official release prints biblical devotional lyrics and credits voices/guitars, keyboards, bass and drums, with a separate string-section credit on its opening track. The authored core arrangement uses a workstation for keyboard-orchestral colors behind distorted riffs and harsh vocals. The boundary is Christian textual identity combined with symphonic layering; this selected black/death-metal branch overlaps those styles and does not claim that every Christian symphonic band has this vocal delivery. The core model does not purport to reproduce the opening track’s live strings. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Renascent — Praise of the Lord God Almighty"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
