  "cypriot_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.power","axes":{"harm":2,"pitch":1,"ornament":1,"meter":2,"density":2,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":2,"timbre":1,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Cypriot metal is a national-scene umbrella, represented by Arrayan Path’s epic heavy/power-metal branch. The label credits guitars, bass, drums, vocals and session keyboards, and emphasizes melodic choruses, galloping sections and vocal projection. The authored arrangement centers those core-band roles with keyboard support. The country identifies the scene, not a compulsory ethnic instrument or a single musical grammar. Arrayan Path’s album-specific oud and bowed-tambur additions are not treated as universal to Cypriot metal, and this core model does not reconstruct those tracks. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Arrayan Path"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "deep_folk_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.folkMetal","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":2,"density":2,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Deep folk metal is treated here as a discovery-metadata cohort, represented by the explicitly credited folk-metal ensemble of Svartby. Its own release notes identify guitars, bass, drums, vocals and keyboards, with Swedish/English fantasy storytelling. The authored realization gives keyboard-led folk-like melody an energetic distorted-guitar and drum foundation. Deep is retained as the allocation’s discovery qualifier, with no invented acoustic definition or claim of a separate historical folk tradition. The selected practice is playful, rhythmically active folk metal, not an unsupported rule that deep folk metal must be slow, meditative or use live folk instruments. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Svartby — Swamp, My Neighbour"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
