  "deep_symphonic_black_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.symphonic","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":1,"density":2,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":2,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Deep symphonic black metal is treated as a discovery cohort, represented by Suffering Souls. Label credits establish guitar, bass, voice and orchestral arrangements by Tobias Micko, with live drums by Michiel van der Plicht. The authored realization couples rapid guitar textures and harsh voice with a keyboard-workstation realization of the orchestral layer. Deep marks the discovery category, not an independently documented historical school. Symphonic refers to the compositional orchestral layer, not proof that every string or choir is a live ensemble; this model stays within the documented black-metal/symphonic overlap. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Suffering Souls — An Iconic Taste of Demise"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "depressive_black_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.black","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":-1,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":1,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Depressive black metal is represented by Austere’s long-form, emotionally bleak black-metal practice. The label describes layered guitars, expressive drums, keyboards and voices; the duo’s own interview stresses dark emotional expression while resisting rigid genre boundaries. The authored arrangement uses repeated melodic guitar figures, spacious keyboard support and restrained-to-intense percussion. Depressive identifies expressive and thematic emphasis; it is neither a diagnosis of musicians or listeners nor a mandatory self-harm theme. It overlaps atmospheric and emotional black metal rather than creating a hard technical boundary. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Austere — Corrosion of Hearts"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "downtempo_deathcore": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.death","axes":{"harm":-1,"pitch":-2,"ornament":0,"meter":1,"density":1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":2,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Downtempo deathcore is represented by Bound in Fear, identified as a Farnham downtempo/deathcore group in its label’s official announcement. The artist profile credits vocals, guitar, bass and drums. The authored realization emphasizes low clipped guitar attacks, widely spaced half-time accents and harsh lead voice, with silence between attacks contributing to weight. The central distinction from fast deathcore is the slow, breakdown-centered rhythmic emphasis, not a claim that every passage is slow or a particular extreme tuning is mandatory. The selected Drop B is an authored playable baseline rather than a transcription of the band’s actual tuning. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Bound in Fear"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "edinburgh_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.postMetal","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":1,"meter":0,"density":1,"transmission":-1,"improv":1,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Edinburgh metal is a city-scene umbrella, represented by DVNE’s progressive post-metal practice. The label credits guitars, bass, drums, keyboards and voices, and quotes the band’s wish for distinct guitar parts, defined bass/drums and clear synths. This authored arrangement uses dynamic heavy/light contrast and evolving melodic riffs with keyboard atmosphere. The city defines the discovery cohort, not a uniquely Edinburgh guitar tone. DVNE’s progressive post-metal branch is one local realization and does not stand in for every Edinburgh heavy-music style. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["DVNE — Voidkind"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "emotional_black_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.black","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":1,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":1,"cyclicity":2},"description":"Emotional black metal is represented by Waldgeflüster’s self-described emotional, nature-connected black-metal practice. Dahoam credits guitar/voice, further guitars, bass, drums, keys and samples, and explores belonging and home through personal reflection. The authored realization balances repeated melodic guitar textures and harsh vocal urgency with quieter space and subtle keyboard layers. Emotional is an explicitly artist-used expressive description, overlapping atmospheric and depressive black metal. It does not mean that other black metal is emotionless, and this nature/home-centered example does not require depressive or self-harm subject matter. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Waldgeflüster — Dahoam"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
