  "minnesota_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.death","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":-1,"ornament":2,"meter":1,"density":2,"transmission":-1,"improv":0,"soundTech":1,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"Minnesota metal is a regional-scene umbrella, represented by the melodic death metal of Majesties. The release credits two guitar roles, bass, drums and vocals; the label emphasizes harmonized leads and melodic writing within aggressive death-metal riffing. The authored arrangement concentrates on those electric-band roles. The location groups musicians rather than prescribing one sound. This Minneapolis-rooted realization is distinct from Minnesota sludge, doom or metalcore; its Swedish stylistic influence does not relocate its documented writing practice to Sweden. The prescribed pickup family, string tuning, studio chain and numeric axes are authored choices for a new recording, not equipment facts about the exemplar.","exemplars":["Majesties — Vast Reaches Unclaimed"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
