  "progressive_deathcore": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.prog","axes":{"harm":1,"pitch":-1,"ornament":1,"meter":0,"density":2,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":2,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Electric guitar and bass support a wide-ranging voice, synthesized layers and programmed percussion, with djembe color in quieter transitions. The official release credits guitar, bass, voices, synthesizer, djembe and programming; this realization uses a sampled drum machine for programmed percussion and an analog-poly synth for unspecified synthesizer hardware. It does not substitute an undocumented live drummer. Sectional contrast and a recurring dramatic arc distinguish the chosen arrangement. D-standard guitar, device type, hand-drum materials and exact patterns are authored.","exemplars":["Slice the Cake — Odyssey to the West"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":["distortedRock.metal.death","distortedRock.punk"]},
  "progressive_groove_metal": {"parent":"distortedRock.metal.prog","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":-1,"ornament":1,"meter":0,"density":1,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":2,"intensity":2,"voice":1,"timbre":2,"percussion":2,"cyclicity":1},"description":"A tight electric-guitar chug is set against moving electric-bass lines and intricate drum accents, opening space for contrast between melodic singing and harsh voice. The label explicitly uses progressive groove metal and documents these roles. This realization favors shifting accents and bass/guitar interplay rather than uninterrupted high-speed runs. Drop-C tuning, humbucker hardware and contemporary production are authored choices.","exemplars":["Jinjer — Wallflowers / Duél"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
