  "jaw_harp": {"parent":"droneModal","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":0,"voice":-2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"The artist labels this exact track jaw-harp solo. The album identifies every jaw harp as made by Zoltán Szilágyi. Manufacturer documentation establishes the Hungarian doromb construction and finger-plucked, oral-resonator technique. Exact solo-track scope excludes violin, singing and drums credited elsewhere on the parent album. This is a Hungarian doromb branch of the broad jaw-harp category, not a Sakha khomus simply because the concert occurred in Yakutia. Source supplies no exact model; manufacturer steel construction and technique are an authored representative realization. Existing regional jaw-harp cards lack a Hungarian doromb form; an isolated new instrument is declared separately. Representative authored present-day recording arrangement for the selected documented branch. Sources establish category, roles and locality. Exact materials, makes, playing settings, tuning, room, signal chain and axes are authored choices, not measured source-session facts or universal genre characteristics.","exemplars":["Áron Szilágyi — Owa (Live in Khampa)"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
