  "japanese_vtuber": {"parent":"functionalSong","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":0,"voice":-2,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Yamaha explicitly publishes the complete six-page intermediate solo-piano edition, composer/lyricist Tsumiki and arranger Miyuki Uchida. Its performance notes describe rhythmic left-hand motion, crisp short notes, selective pedal and a reworked accompaniment for the rap-like E section. This whole published arrangement is selected, not an isolated piano reduction claimed to reconstruct the original studio master. One piano performer covers melody and accompaniment; no separately notated singer is specified by the solo edition. The original song singer and composer are not counted as performers of this authored piano realization. Hololive directly identifies Hoshimachi Suisei as its virtual idol and its institutional VTuber production article explicitly identifies her collaboration with Tsumiki on BIBBIDIBA. Japanese VTuber describes the avatar-mediated streaming talent and creator institution, not a universal instrument palette. Actual existing vocaloid_synth_voice and vocaloid_producer_scene center synthesized voicebanks; shared creators do not make this talent institution identical to that production mechanism. Existing anime_cv centers anime-character songs and j_pop_classic the broad mainstream agency/pop lineage, both overlapping repertoire contexts but not synonymous with the VTuber institution. This selected published J-pop song arrangement uses broad functionalSong with an explicitly authored functional-harmonic verse/refrain realization, not a measured transcription claim about every original section and not art-music classification merely from notation. Steinway D nine-foot concert grand, block-chord pop keyboard articulation, modern piano wire/felt and equal temperament are authored representative construction choices, not claims about the original singer recording or Yamaha specifying that piano model. Controlled live-room capture is likewise authored.","exemplars":["Hoshimachi Suisei / Tsumiki — BIBBIDIBA, complete Miyuki Uchida Yamaha six-page solo-piano arrangement"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
  "kazakh_indie": {"parent":"balladPoetry","axes":{"harm":0,"pitch":0,"ornament":0,"meter":0,"density":-1,"transmission":0,"improv":0,"soundTech":0,"intensity":0,"voice":0,"timbre":0,"percussion":-1,"cyclicity":0},"description":"Documented initial solo performance and prior solo songwriter practice of Galymzhan Moldanazar, Almaty, February2015. In a firsthand interview, collaborator Ivan Trevino describes their first meeting in Chaz Martin’s living room: Moldanazar sat, played his guitar and softly sang a song before the subsequent joint rehearsals. The artist separately describes his usual earlier practice as singing with his guitar. This complete solo practice is selected, not an instrument-stripped version of later Akpen Birge with Break of Reality, the New York recording, or the later Moldanazar band. Exactly one singer and one guitar; song title at the initial encounter is not supplied. No listening or exact original guitar construction is claimed. Exact creator Kazakh Indie playlist positively includes Moldanazar at item10. Firsthand artist and collaborator testimony identifies an independent self-written Kazakh-language songwriter path, moving from solo songs to an indie band and international collaboration. This is a national independent-music scene and discovery network, with folk, rock and electronic branches and substantial overlap with wider Kazakh popular music. Existing kazakh_pop is a broad national label represented by Q-pop/Ninety One, not falsely restricted to only its example; the independent songwriter/band community is the narrower overlapping boundary, not merely a different instrument palette. Existing kazakh_hip_hop covers the national rap field, not every independent musician, and kazakh_traditional describes historical steppe song/kuy rather than this contemporary independent songwriting community. Selected lyric-led minimal solo accompaniment fits the broad balladPoetry node; it is not assigned an Anglophone child or claimed to represent every Kazakh indie arrangement. Authored intimate acoustic songwriter rendition preserves sole accompanied voice and guitar. A steel-string OM with mahogany top/back/sides, phosphor-bronze strings, standard guitar tuning and flatpicked melodic accompaniment is an editorial realization of the positively documented guitar role, not an assertion of source model, material, strings or exact gesture. Source-unspecified voice physiology, single natural lead and controlled live room are authored defaults. No global temperament or original capture hardware is asserted.","exemplars":["Galymzhan Moldanazar — documented early solo voice-and-guitar practice and Almaty living-room encounter (February2015)"],"status":"documented","crossRefs":[]},
